# WNBA Analytics Agent

The Analytics Agent precomputes every derived statistic into database tables so
API responses never depend on request-time math. It is a deterministic in-app
pipeline: `app/Services/WNBA/Agents/AggregateComputationService.php`, queued
via `app/Jobs/RunAnalyticsAgent.php`, triggered by the nightly data-agent chain,
`app:wnba-agent analytics`, or `POST /api/wnba/data/agent-run`.

Consumers read via `app/Services/WNBA/Analytics/AggregateStatsReader.php` (or
models directly). Missing aggregate rows must surface as `null` / empty — never
fake league-average placeholders (e.g. DRtg `100`).

## Output tables (written ONLY by this agent)

- `wnba_player_season_stats` — totals, per-game averages, shooting
  percentages, home/away + per-36 splits (one row per player per season)
- `wnba_team_season_stats` — record, pace, off/def/net rating, Four Factors
  (own + opponent), home/away splits
- `wnba_player_game_advanced` — per game: TS%, eFG%, usage%, game score,
  points per shot, decimal minutes
- `wnba_matchup_summaries` — head-to-head per season: wins, avg total, avg
  margin, avg pace, recent meetings
- `wnba_player_vs_defense` — player splits by opponent team DRtg bucket
  (`elite` &lt; 95, `good` 95–105, `average` 105–110, `poor` ≥ 110)
- `wnba_player_performance_trends` — windows `l5` / `l10` / `season`: avgs +
  linear slopes for PTS/REB/AST
- `wnba_team_performance_trends` — windows `l5` / `l10` / `season`: W-L,
  PPG for/against, pace, ORtg/DRtg over the window

API controllers read these tables (see `PlayerController::leaders`, player
analytics `vs_defense` / `performance_trends`, matchup + game preview). New
derived stats belong in these tables (or a new agent-owned table), not in
controllers.

## Formula conventions (formula_version `v1-box-estimate`)

- Percentages are decimals 0..1. Safe division: denominator 0 → `null`,
  never 0 or NaN. `null` inputs propagate to `null` outputs.
- Possessions (box estimate, matches `TeamAnalyticsService`):
  `FGA + 0.44·FTA − ORB + TOV`. WNBA games are 40 minutes (200 team minutes).
- TS% = PTS / (2·(FGA + 0.44·FTA)); eFG% = (FGM + 0.5·3PM) / FGA.
- Usage% (box estimate): `(FGA + 0.44·FTA + TOV)·(TeamMin/5) / (MP·(TmFGA + 0.44·TmFTA + TmTOV))`.
- Game Score: Hollinger formula.
- Ratings: points (allowed) × 100 / possessions; net = off − def.
  Team season DRtg uses **opponent** possessions.
- Matchup difficulty (read-time lookup only): compare opponent team DRtg to
  league median (±3 band) → `favorable` | `neutral` | `difficult`.
- Every aggregate row records `formula_version`, `computed_at`, and
  `agent_run_id`. If you change a formula, bump the version string and
  recompute — never mix versions within a table silently.

## Input discipline

- Inputs are the canonical tables (`wnba_player_games`, `wnba_game_teams`,
  `wnba_games`), excluding rows with `validation_status = 'invalid'` and DNP
  rows, and excluding 0-0 placeholder game-team rows (scheduled games).
- Players/teams with open identity conflicts in `wnba_data_conflicts`
  (`requires_review = true`, unresolved) are skipped so a mis-mapped entity
  cannot poison aggregates; the skip is counted in the run summary.
- `computePlayerVsDefense` runs after `computeTeamSeasonStats` so opponent
  DRtg buckets are available; games vs teams without a season row are skipped.
- Adjusted plus-minus / RAPM-style metrics and defense-vs-position are out of
  scope for v1 (needs PBP stints / richer roles); raw plus-minus comes straight
  from box scores.

## Run contract

Runs record counters (`player_season_stats_computed`,
`player_vs_defense_computed`, `player_performance_trends_computed`,
`team_performance_trends_computed`, etc.) to `wnba_agent_runs` via
`AgentRunReporter`. Recomputation is idempotent (`updateOrCreate` on natural
keys) — recomputing a season with unchanged inputs yields identical rows.
After a successful run the response cache is cleared so the API serves fresh
aggregates.

**After deploy:** run `php artisan app:wnba-agent analytics` (or
`POST /api/wnba/data/agent-run`) for the current season so the three new
tables are populated before traffic depends on them.
